    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/security/path-containment.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "",
      "prov:value": "---\nname: path-containment\ndescription: >\n  Turning a value from outside into a path. The two different questions —\n  a URL path versus a single identifier — why collapsing them is a defect,\n  and the three sinks in this repository that had neither check.\nconsulted: true\n---"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/security/path-containment.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Path containment — two questions that look like one",
      "prov:value": "**The lexical check is the weaker half.** `resolve` is string arithmetic and\nnever touches the filesystem, so a symlink inside the root pointing out of it\npasses. Recorded in `serve-rendering.ts`: the first version of its resolver\nreturned **200** for exactly that, found by its own test rather than by review.\n`realPathWithin` is the half that catches it, and `writableWithin` walks up to\nthe nearest existing ancestor because a target that does not exist yet has no\nrealpath to compare."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/security/path-containment.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Path containment — two questions that look like one",
      "prov:value": "## Measured, 2026-09-25 — the three sinks that had nothing (bean `6bhf`)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 6bhf",
        "2026-09-25"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-25"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/security/path-containment.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Measured, 2026-09-25 — the three sinks that had nothing (bean `6bhf`)",
      "prov:value": "| route | sink | primitive |\n|---|---|---|\n| `POST /api/import/arxiv` | `join(UPLOADS_DIR(), id)` → `mkdirSync(recursive)` + `writeFileSync` | arbitrary directory creation and file write |\n| `GET /api/feedback?paperId=` | `feedbackPath` → `join(base, paperId, rootName + \".ts\")` | read outside the store |\n| `POST /api/feedback` | `writeFeedback` → `mkdirSync` + `writeFileSync` | write outside the store |"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/security/path-containment.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Measured, 2026-09-25 — the three sinks that had nothing (bean `6bhf`)",
      "prov:value": "## Then two MORE sinks, 2026-09-26 — and this is the lesson, not the list",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-26"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-26"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/security/path-containment.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The gate, and what it cannot do",
      "prov:value": "`scripts/tests/server-path-sinks.test.ts` — 8 of its 13 tests fail against the\npre-fix server and all 13 pass after, verified by reverting the file. It is a\n**source ratchet** and says so: it proves the guard has not been deleted, never\nthat a value is checked on every path to a sink. It asserts its own non-vacuity,\nbecause a renamed server would otherwise make every `not.toContain` pass."
    }
  ]
